/-
# HC Gap L4 -- Front C92: Cartan generator line criterion (R656).

R655 identifies the live target with the Cartan scalar-preimage theorem:
every class in `trivialModulePart` must be `j_q (r • h^4)`.

This file makes that target more concrete without adding a new assumption.
The Cartan H8 source is already `span {h^4}`, and Borel stable-range
injectivity makes `j_q(h^4)` non-zero.  Therefore its image is exactly the
one-dimensional line `span {j_q(h^4)}`.  The remaining target is the geometric
containment

  `trivialModulePart <= span {j_q(h^4)}`.

That containment is equivalent to the scalar-preimage theorem, and hence to
the R655 bijectivity/right-inverse target after the source carrier is fixed.
-/

import HodgeReduction.HCGapL4.FrontC91_H8ResidualRightInverseScalarPreimageEquivalence

set_option linter.dupNamespace false

namespace HodgeReduction
namespace HCGapL4
